BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bvbrief-20260910-cscouncil@brazosvalley
DTSTAMP:20260913T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260910T220000
SUMMARY:College Station City Council - regular meeting (HELD)
LOCATION:City Hall Council Chambers\, 1101 Texas Ave.\, College Station
DESCRIPTION:HELD. The Bass Pro Shops and Corinth Group agreements were reviewed in workshop with no vote\; action is set for September 24. The council approved a $23\,090\,000 contract with CSA Construction for Carters Creek WWTP Enhanced Filtration plus a $2\,309\,000 contingency. Mayor Nichols was absent. Tracker BV-0220 through BV-0224.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bvbrief-20260915-bryancouncil-special@brazosvalley
DTSTAMP:20260920T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260915T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260915T190000
SUMMARY:Bryan City Council - special meeting (HELD)
LOCATION:Bryan Municipal Building\, 300 S. Texas Ave.\, Bryan
DESCRIPTION:The council adopted a 2026 property tax rate of $0.624000 per $100 at second and final reading\, unanimously on a roll-call vote\, and ratified the property tax revenue increase. It approved a $350\,000 Chapter 380 agreement with N N Out Properties for the Bryan Hotel and the Ryan Building\, an eleven-item consent agenda\, and the appointment of Pete Bienski as BTU board chair. No action was announced on the SMBG Bryan executive-session subject. Tracker BV-0236 through BV-0239.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
