SUMMARY:Brazos County Commissioners Court - regular agenda session (HELD)
LOCATION:Administration Building\, 200 South Texas Avenue\, Suite 106\, Bryan
DESCRIPTION:The court sent RFP #26-088 for grant writing back to committee\, a second deferral\; approved $484\,600 and $500\,000 change orders on two building renovations\; adopted a 6 percent Local Provider Participation Fund rate\; approved twenty fiscal 2027 community support contracts and five plats\; and took no action out of a closed session on the county manager\, the director of project management and the Easterwood Airport contract. Tracker BV-0246 through BV-0251.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bvbrief-20260921-marion-pugh@brazosvalley
DTSTAMP:20260920T100000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:Marion Pugh Drive full closure begins in College Station
LOCATION:Marion Pugh Drive from the Stadium View southern exit to south of Luther Street\, College Station
DESCRIPTION:Full closure for about two weeks while crews install water\, wastewater and storm crossings. Luther Street stays closed through Phase 3A\, now estimated at 10 to 12 weeks. Phase 3B follows on the east side for six to eight weeks with a single southbound lane open. The project is expected to finish in early January. Tracker BV-0257.
END:VEVENT
